{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context and intent\n\nRetire the two bridge verbs that were dead on arrival: `rebar bridge-status` and\n`rebar purge-bridge`. This pure dead-code deletion was carved out of\n`4752-3afb-e8bd-448a` so it could land independently; nothing in the new `bridge`\nsurface replaces either verb.\n\n`bridge-status` consumed `<tracker>/.bridge-status.json`, but this repository never\ncontained a producer and the command exited 1 on post-cutover repositories. Its module\nalso carried a dangling `epic 3a03` citation. `purge-bridge` had no script, workflow,\nor runbook caller and exposed an inverted-sense `--keep` flag. Neither command warranted\na compatibility alias or deprecation forwarder.\n\n## Completed implementation\n\nGerrit change 1517 (`Ic40ab04419a5ebfb4e0b6486cb1272309f4dfc67`) merged to\n`main` on 2026-08-07 after `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, and zero unresolved\ncomments. The merged implementation has these observable end states:\n\n- CLI wiring in `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py` contains only the surviving\n  `bridge-fsck` entry in `_BRIDGE`; the `bridge-status` and `purge-bridge` dispatch\n  arms are absent. Top-level `rebar doctor` remains unchanged.\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge.py` and\n  `src/rebar/_commands/purge_bridge.py` are absent, with no shims or aliases.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge-status.txt`,\n  `src/rebar/_cli/help/purge-bridge.txt`, and both overview entries are absent.\n- `src/rebar/schemas/bridge_status.schema.json`, the `BRIDGE_STATUS` export and\n  constant, and the `OUTPUT_SCHEMAS[\"bridge_status\"]` entry are absent.\n- The retired-only tests are absent:\n  `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_status.py`,\n  `tests/unit/test_purge_bridge_locked_commit.py`,\n  `tests/interfaces/store/test_purge_bridge_prune_concurrency.py`, and\n  `tests/interfaces/store/_purge_race_worker.py`.\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_schema_coverage.py` has no retired schema\n  exemption. `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py` asserts both\n  tokens are retired. `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_alert_display.py` positively\n  verifies neutral guidance from both surviving bridge-alert warning paths.\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads_cli.py` names no retired or not-yet-shipped\n  command, and `src/rebar/_engine_support/output.py` no longer documents a\n  `bridge-status` report profile.\n- Active command documentation was updated in `docs/cli-reference.md`,\n  `docs/exit-codes.md`, and `docs/output-schemas.md`.\n- `CHANGELOG.md` records the breaking removals. `docs/release-notes.md` is an\n  enumerated, intentional consumer: it records the agent-visible removal of both\n  commands and the `bridge_status` output schema. Those historical retirement names\n  are expected there and are not stale live-surface references.\n- `.github/complexity-baseline.json` carries the resulting shrink of `_dispatch`.\n\nNo persisted ticket data, migration, external integration, auth boundary, or shared\nstate format changed.\n\n## Verification evidence\n\n- Held-out retirement contract: 7/7 tests passed. Restoring `bridge-status` made the\n  oracle fail, and the refactoring litmus passed.\n- Focused post-rebase contracts: 41 passed across help, schema, and alert-display tests.\n- Local gates: `make lint` passed; `make typecheck` passed across 437 source files.\n- Full pre-rebase suite: 11,149 passed, 40 skipped, 228 deselected.\n- Exact patch-set-2 CI run 31218769114 passed artifact provenance, optionality,\n  dependency audit, identity, ticket resolution, golden path, lint/typecheck, and all\n  macOS/Ubuntu Python 3.11/3.12/3.13 test matrices.\n- The behavioral oracle proves both retired tokens take the unknown-command path and\n  are absent from top-level help. Live package and command-contract surfaces contain\n  no `bridge-status` or `purge-bridge` references. Tests, changelogs, archives, and the\n  explicit retirement notice in `docs/release-notes.md` retain intentional history.\n\n## Rollback\n\nIf an undiscovered downstream consumer still invokes either retired verb, revert\nGerrit change 1517. No data migration or persisted-format reversal is required.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `rebar bridge-status` exits as an unknown command.\n- [x] `rebar purge-bridge` exits as an unknown command.\n- [x] Neither retired command appears in `rebar --help`.\n- [x] Both implementation modules are deleted without shims or aliases.\n- [x] The retired schema and every `BRIDGE_STATUS` registry surface are absent.\n- [x] Surviving read warnings provide neutral bridge-alert guidance.\n- [x] The package/help/active-command-doc oracle passes, with historical evidence\n      explicitly scoped and retained.\n- [x] Retired-only tests are deleted and replacement behavioral contracts pass.\n- [x] Active command docs, `CHANGELOG.md`, and `docs/release-notes.md` record the\n      correct post-removal contract.\n- [x] The dangling `epic 3a03` citation disappeared with its retired module.\n- [x] `bridge-fsck` and top-level `rebar doctor` behavior remain intact."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786139354661613001,"uuid":"ceb90b27-b74b-4f52-9207-ad7ed4904485"}